Reuses the existing trip_exceptions infrastructure (Part 1) rather than
building a parallel system:

- DB: widened trip_exceptions.type to add route_deviation, unplanned_stop,
  delay, gps_failure, tracking_failure, sync_failure. Added lat/lng
  (every exception now carries a location). Added a partial unique index
  on (trip_id, type) where status='open' for the 6 new types — a real
  DB-level guarantee against duplicate exceptions, not just an app-side
  check. Added mcc_centres.route_deviation_threshold_m (default 300) and
  unplanned_stop_minutes (default 5), same owner-configurable pattern as
  Phase 5's timing thresholds.
- src/lib/geo.ts: distanceToPathMeters() — point-to-polyline distance.
- src/lib/route-exceptions.ts: pure detectRouteDeviation() and
  detectUnplannedStop(), both requiring 2 consecutive pings before
  flagging (same jitter filter as Phase 6's arrival/departure detection).
- src/lib/exceptions.ts: single source of truth for the exception type
  vocabulary + labels; manager.tsx's local duplicate copy removed.
- live.tsx: detection candidates for the focused agent — deviation and
  unplanned-stop from the new detectors; delay reuses Phase 5's
  classification as-is; gps_failure/tracking_failure reuse
  tracking_sessions.status/failure_reason (Phase 2) as-is. A best-effort
  effect logs each newly-detected condition once per trip (guarded by the
  DB unique index against races). New 'Open exceptions' panel in Agent
  Detail with a Resolve action (status/resolved_at/resolved_by, same
  pattern as quality.tsx's alert resolution).

Known limitation (stated, not hidden): detection only runs while a
manager has that agent focused on the live map — there is no background
job in this architecture. sync_failure is in the type vocabulary for
forward compatibility but has no detector yet; that's Phase 8's job,
once an actual offline/sync queue for gps_pings exists.
